false_positive_filter.rust_note:
Python `$` (no MULTILINE) also matches before a final '
'. The values reaching this filter come from `[^\s'";
]{3,}` and never contain '
', so the original regex behaves the same in Rust; the `
?$` spelling is given for exactness if the filter is reused elsewhere. `^` without MULTILINE means start of string in both engines.
